  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, thanks for letting us know. I checked your laptop (BL-LT-0101) and it's actually in good shape right now. It has about 310 GB free out of 512 GB, which is roughly 60%, and it isn't showing any warnings. Before we change anything, could you help me figure out where the message came from? 1) Is the warning still showing up, and when did you last see it? 2) Could you send a screenshot of it? It would help to know which drive it names (for example C: or D:). 3) Did it appear on this laptop, or on another computer or a USB or external drive? 4) Was it right after a big download, sync, or update? It may have been a short-lived spike that has since cleared. If it comes back, emptying the Recycle Bin and Downloads folder and running Disk Cleanup will usually free up space quickly. Once I hear back, I'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket: user reports a Windows low-disk-space warning and asks for cleanup. User is Dana Whitfield, CEO (VIP), and has one device, BL-LT-0101. Latest device check-in (2026-10-11 02:54 UTC): online, 512 GB total, 310 GB free (60.5%), no warnings. That's far above KB-017's 10% threshold, so the reported symptom doesn't match current telemetry. Possible explanations: a temporary spike that has cleared (e.g. a OneDrive sync or update), a secondary/external drive, a different machine, or a misread notification. I took no action. Waiting on the user for a screenshot, the drive letter, and which device. If it turns out to be BL-LT-0101 with low space confirmed, follow the KB-017 cleanup steps. If the warning keeps appearing while telemetry shows plenty of free space, escalate to Tier 2 as a possible reporting/agent discrepancy. VIP: please prioritise follow-up.",
